cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Periodic Table of DFIR
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Marino
    family-names: Bekios
    website: https://marinobekios.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7778-5035
repository-code: https://github.com/ledlight33/periodic-table-of-dfir
url: https://ledlight33.github.io/periodic-table-of-dfir/
abstract: >-
  A visual reference of 126 tools for Digital Forensics and Incident Response,
  organised in the structure of the periodic table across ten categories, with
  a synthetic elements row for the emerging generation of AI assisted DFIR
  tooling. Published as an interactive web page, printable A1 and A3 editions,
  and a machine readable dataset.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
  - DFIR
  - cybersecurity
  - threat intelligence
  - malware analysis
  - mobile forensics
  - cloud forensics
  - taxonomy
  - visual reference
